0289 | \section{Churro-waffle space is quasi-isometry invariant}\label{sec:churrowaffle}
0290 | For \grsg-group $\Gamma$, the space $\Ugos{\gog{J}}$ has underlying tree structure $T_{\gog{J}}$, with churros attached to crêpes along lines of line patterns. From Proposition \ref{prop:combinatorialize}, for each crêpe $\crepe=\left(\pcdisc,\Line\right)$ there is waffle $\waffle$ with hyperplanes $\hypplane{\Line}$ quasimatching $\Line$. The vertex group $\Gamma_{\crepe}$ acts properly and cocompactly by isometries on $\waffle$, with each adjacent vertex group $\Gamma_{\churro}$ stabilizing a hyperplane $\hypplane{\gamma}$, where $\churro\subset\Ugos{\gog{J}}$ is attached along $\gamma\in\Line$. Furthermore, if $H$ and $\Gamma$ are quasi-isometric \grsg-groups, then waffles for corresponding vertices (as in Lemma \ref{lem:qi1}) are isometric.
0291 | 
0292 | We would like to build a tree of spaces by attaching churros to waffles, following $T_{\gog{J}}$, in order to obtain a space on which $\Gamma$ acts by isometry. However, this creates a problem: how are we supposed to
0293 | attach churros to these hyperplanes?
0294 | 
0295 | It follows from Sageev's work
0296 | that these hyperplanes are themselves $\cato$-cube complexes. We will
0297 | therefore use $\cato$ geometry to show the existence of a canonical
0298 | geodesic within each hyperplane along which we can attach a churro
0299 | flap.
0300 | 
0301 | \subsection{Attaching churros to waffles: strands}\label{sec:strands}
0302 | 
0303 | 
0304 | \begin{prop}[Strands of 2-ended $\cato$ spaces]\label{prop:strands}
0305 | 	Let $X$ be a 2-ended $\cato$ metric space and let $\Gamma$ be a
0306 | 	group that acts properly and cocompactly on $X$ by isometries. There
0307 | 	is a canonical geodesic $\sigma:\bbR \to X$ called the
0308 | 	\define{$\Gamma$-strand} of $X$ with the property that
0309 | 	$\Gamma \cdot \sigma = \sigma$. Furthermore $\sigma$ is an axis of
0310 | 	translation for every hyperbolic isometry of $X$.
0311 | \end{prop}
