0318 | \begin{defn}[Types of 2-ended groups]\label{defn:2e-types}
0319 | 	Let $\Gamma$ be 2-ended group, then either it maps onto $\bbZ$, in
0320 | 	which case we say it is of \define{$\bbZ$-type} or it maps onto $D_\infty = \bbZ \rtimes
0321 | 	\bbZ/2\bbZ$ in which case we say it is of \define{dihedral type}. If
0322 | 	$\Gamma$ is of dihedral type, we denote by $\Gamma^+$ the preimage of
0323 | 	the maximal infinite cyclic subgroup of $D_\infty$, otherwise let $\Gamma^+=\Gamma$.
0324 | \end{defn}
0325 | 
0326 | In the $\bbZ$-type case, Proposition \ref{prop:strands} will follow
0327 | almost immediately from the two results cited below. For the dihedral
0328 | case a bit more work will be needed.
0329 | 
0330 | \begin{prop}[see {\cite[Proposition II.2.7]{bridson2011metric}}]\label{prop:cato-centre}
0331 | 	Let $X$ be a complete $\cato$ space. If $Y\subset X$ is a bounded
0332 | 	set or radius $r_y$, then there exists a unique point $c_Y \in X$,
0333 | 	called the centre of $Y$, such that $Y \subset \overline{B}(c_y,r_y)$.
0334 | \end{prop}
