0447 | \begin{lem}\label{lem:strand-classification}
0448 | 	Let $\strand \subset \waffle$ be a strand corresponding to a
0449 | 	hyperplane in a waffle $\waffle$, and let $K\leq
0450 | 	\Isom\waffle$ act cocompactly on $\waffle$. Then the stabilizer
0451 | 	$K_\strand$ is one of the following types:
0452 | 	\begin{enumerate}
0453 | 		\item $\bbZ$-type,
0454 | 		\item dihedral type, or
0455 | 		\item\label{it:reflective} isomorphic to $\bbZ \oplus \bbZ_2$ or
0456 | 		$(\bbZ\semidirect\bbZ_2) \oplus \bbZ_2$.
0457 | 	\end{enumerate}
0458 | 	In the latter case the $\bbZ_2$ factor fixes $\sigma$ pointwise.
0459 | \end{lem}
0460 | \begin{proof}
0461 | 	If $K_\strand$ acts freely on $\strand$, then it is of $\bbZ$-type.
0462 | 	Let $\strand^\pm$ be the endpoints of $\strand \in \partial\waffle$
0463 | 	and suppose that some elements of $K_\strand$ fix a point $x$ of
0464 | 	$\strand.$ Then any such elements induce isometries of the circle
0465 | 	$\partial\waffle$ with respect to the visual metric based at $x$ and
0466 | 	permute $\strand^\pm$ or the connected components of the complement
0467 | 	$\partial \waffle\setminus\left\{\strand^\pm\right\}$. Because
0468 | 	elements of $K$ are fully determined by their action on
0469 | 	$\partial\waffle$, it follows that
0470 | 	$(K_\strand)_x \leq \bbZ_2 \oplus \bbZ_2$, so it either has
0471 | 	cardinality 1,2 or 4.
0472 | 
0473 | 	Now $K_\sigma$ acts discretely cocompactly on $\strand$ by
0474 | 	isometries, therefore the quotient $K_\strand\backslash\strand$ is
0475 | 	either a circle or a closed segment. If the quotient is a circle,
0476 | 	then any element that fixes some point in $\strand$, must fix
0477 | 	$\strand$ pointwise, so $K_\strand \approx \bbZ \oplus
0478 | 	\bbZ_2$. Otherwise there is some $K_x \leq K_\strand$ that permutes
0479 | 	the endpoints $\strand^\pm$. If $|K_x|=4$ then there must also be
0480 | 	some element $k$ that fixes $\strand^\pm$ and therefore $\strand$
0481 | 	pointwise, but permutes the connected components of
0482 | 	$\partial\waffle\setminus\{\strand^\pm\}$, so that $K_\strand =
0483 | 	(\bbZ\semidirect\bbZ_2) \oplus \bbZ_2$. If $|K_x|=2$ then $K_\strand
0484 | 	= \bbZ\semidirect\bbZ_2$.
0485 | \end{proof}
