0544 | \begin{defn}[Horostrip]\label{defn:horostrip}
0545 |   Consider the upper half plane model of $\bbH^2$, the hyperbolic
0546 |   2-space. For $0<y_1<y_2$ the \define{horostrip} $\panel(y_1,y_2)$ is
0547 |   the closed region bounded by the
0548 |   lines\[ y= y_1 \textrm{~and~} y=y_2.\] The lines in
0549 |   $\panel(y_1,y_2)$ parallel to the $y$-axis are called
0550 |   \define{vertical leaves.} The quantity $|\ln(y_2/y_1)|$ is called
0551 |   the \define{width} of $\panel(y_1,y_2).$ The boundary component
0552 |   contained in $\{(x,y)\mid y = y_1\}$ is called the \define{long side}.
0553 | 
