0665 | \subsubsection{The path metric on a churro-waffle space}
0666 | 
0667 | Before continuing we note that churros, with the metric of Definition
0668 | \ref{defn:churro-metrization}, may not have isometrically embedded
0669 | boundaries in the following sense: the path metric restricted to the
0670 | boundary (i.e. given by paths lying in the boundary) may not agree
0671 | with the induced subspace metric; the reason being that horospheres
0672 | are not convex.
0673 | 
0674 | \begin{defn}[Global path metric]\label{defn:path-metric.}
0675 |   Let $\chuwaf{\Gamma}$ be the churro-waffle space for a clean group
0676 |   $\Gamma$ where each waffle $\waffle$ is equipped with the standard
0677 |   piecewise Euclidean path metric $ds_{\waffle}$ and each churro
0678 |   $\churro$ is equipped with the path metric $ds_{\churro}$ given in
0679 |   Definition \ref{defn:churro-metrization}. If a churro $\churro$ is
0680 |   adjacent to a waffle $\waffle$ with $\churro \cap \waffle = \strand$
0681 |   we identify the component $\gamma \subset \partial \churro$ with
0682 |   $\strand \subset \waffle$ so that for any arc $\gamma\subset\strand$
0683 |   we have \[
0684 |     \int_\gamma ds_{\waffle} = \int_\gamma ds_{\churro}.
0685 |     \] This induces the \define{global path metric $d$ on $\chuwaf\Gamma$.}
0686 | \end{defn}
0687 | 
0688 | \begin{prop}\label{prop:global-isometry}
0689 |   $\Gamma$ can be made to act by isometries on $\chuwaf\Gamma$ with
0690 |   respect to the global path metric $d$.
0691 | \end{prop}
0692 | \begin{proof}
0693 |   The only fact we actually need to show is that for a churro
0694 |   $\churro$, the stabilizer $\Gamma_\churro = \bk{h_\churro}$ can act
0695 |   by isometries. Indeed, we already know that for each waffle
0696 |   $\waffle$ the path metric is $\Gamma_\waffle$-equivariant, if this
0697 |   is also the case for every churro then, by construction and
0698 |   definition, $\Gamma$ will carry geodesics to geodesics.
0699 | 
0700 |   Let $\{\waffle_i\mid 1\leq i \leq m_\churro\}$ be the set of waffles
0701 |   attached to the churro $\churro$ and let $x \in \churrocore$ be some
0702 |   point in the churro core. Let $x_i \in \waffle_i$ be the point in
0703 |   connected to $x$ via a vertical leaf in the flap $\flap_{i}$
0704 |   connecting $\churrocore$ to $\strand_i \subset \waffle_i$.
0705 | 
0706 |   Let $y_i$ be the point in $\churrocore$ connected to
0707 |   $h_\churro \cdot x_i$ by a vertical leaf in the flap
0708 |   $\flap_{i}$. We note that with respect to the path metric defined in
0709 |   Definition \ref{defn:path-metric.} the length of the arc
0710 |   $\alpha_i \subset \strand_i$ connecting $x_i$ to
0711 |   $h_\churro\cdot x_i$ is exactly $\tau_{\strand_i}$ and by Definition
0712 |   \ref{defn:churro-metrization} and Proposition
0713 |   \ref{prop:quadrilaterals}, with respect to the path metric, in each
0714 |   flap we have that the length of the arc $\beta$ between $x$ and
0715 |   $y_i$ is $\tau_\churrocore$. It follows that restricted to each
0716 |   flap $\flap_i$ the action of $h_\churro$ can be realized as the
0717 |   restriction of a parabolic isometry of the upper half plane model of
0718 |   $\bbH^2$ of the type:
0719 |   \[ (x,y) \mapsto (x+h,y); \textrm{~for some~} h \in \bbR.
0720 |   \] which agree on \[
0721 |     \churrocore = \bigcap_{i=1}^{m_\churro} \flap_i.
0722 |   \] It follows that the length of any parameterized curve can be in
0723 |   $\chuwaf\Gamma$ can be computed using the local path metrics in the
0724 |   churro and waffle pieces and that such lengths are preserved under
0725 |   actions by $\Gamma$.
0726 | \end{proof}
