0810 | \begin{lem}[Assembly Lemma]\label{lem:assemble}
0811 |   Let $H,\Gamma$ be clean $\grsg$-groups and suppose there is a
0812 |   quasi-isometry $\phi:\chuwaf H \to \chuwaf \Gamma$ that satisfies
0813 |   the following:
0814 |   \begin{enumerate}
0815 |   \item\label{lem:assemble-tree} $\phi$ coarsely maps churros to churros and waffles to waffles, which induces an graph isomorphism of the underlying tree structures of $\chuwaf H$ and $\chuwaf \Gamma$.
0816 | 
0817 |   \item\label{lem:assemble-isom} The restriction of $\phi$ to a waffle $\waffle\subset\chuwaf H$ induces an isometry $\sqphi_{\waffle}$ of
0818 |     $\waffle$ with respect to the intrinsic metric.
0819 | 
0820 |   \item\label{lem:assemble-clutch} $\phi$ preserves the clutching ratios of a churro, in that
0821 |   \begin{equation}
0822 |     \label{eq:4}
0823 |     \frac{\tau_{\strand_1}}{\tau_{\strand_2}}=
0824 |     \frac{\tau_{\strand_{1'}}}{\tau_{\strand_{2'}}}.
0825 |   \end{equation}
0826 |   for any pair $\waffle_1,\waffle_2\subset\chuwaf H$ of waffles attached to a churro $\churro$ along strands $\sigma_1,\sigma_2$ respectively, where $\strand_{1'},\strand_{2'}$ are the respective strands along which $\sqphi_{\waffle_1}(\waffle_1),\sqphi_{\waffle_2}(\waffle_2)$ are attached to their shared adjacent churro (which is a bounded distance from $\phi(\churro)$).
0827 | \end{enumerate}
0828 | Then there are families of equivariant generalized Dehn twists $D,E$
0829 | such that $\chuwaf H^D$ and $\chuwaf \Gamma^E$ are isomorphic. Thus
0830 | both $H$ and $\Gamma$ can be made to act freely by automorphisms on the common churro-waffle space $\chuwaf H^D\cong\chuwaf \Gamma^E$
0831 | \end{lem}
0832 | \begin{proof}
0833 |   If we metrize $\chuwaf H$ and $\chuwaf\Gamma$ as in Definition
0834 |   \ref{defn:path-metric.} then by Lemma \ref{lem:ratio} and equation
0835 |   (\ref{eq:4}), the local metrics defined on the churros make
0836 |   $\phi$-correspondent churros isometric. Note that the strands in the
0837 |   waffles only depend on the isometry classes of the waffles, so we
0838 |   can pick strand subdivisions for every waffle that is
0839 |   $\Isom{\waffle}$-equivariant, and pick such a subdivision for every
0840 |   isometry class of waffles occurring in $\chuwaf H$ and $\chuwaf\Gamma$. It now follows by Lemma \ref{lem:partial-twist}, that
0841 |   after performing finitely many equivariant generalized Dehn twists,
0842 |   and redefining the flap subdivision, we can make $\chuwaf H$ and
0843 |   $\chuwaf\Gamma$ isometric as metric spaces and isomorphic as cell
0844 |   complexes.
0845 | \end{proof}
