0894 | 	the \define{$D$-coarse intersection of $\alpha$ and $\beta$}, is the
0895 | 	set of points that are simultaneously at distance $D$ from $\alpha$
0896 | 	and $\beta$,
0897 | 	i.e.\[ \coarseint \alpha D \beta = \left\{x \mid
0898 | 	d(x,\alpha),d(x,\beta)\leq D\right\} = N_{D}(\alpha) \cap
0899 | 	N_{D}(\beta).
