0904 | \begin{lem}\label{lem:coarse-int-finite}
0905 |  If $\alpha,\beta$ are bi-infinite geodesics with distinct endpoints
0906 |  in $\partial X$, then $\coarseint \alpha D \beta$ has finite diameter
0907 |  $M(\alpha,\beta,D)$.
0908 | \end{lem}
0909 | \begin{proof}
0910 |   If $\coarseint \alpha D \beta$ has infinite diameter, then
0911 |   $\alpha,\beta$ must fellow travel to the same point in $\partial
0912 |   X$, contradicting that they have distinct endpoints.
0913 | \end{proof}
