0915 | \begin{lem}\label{lem:global-strand-bound}
0916 |   Let $\strand_1,\strand_2$ be strands in $\waffle$, then for
0917 |   any $D>0$ there is an $N(D)$ such that \[
0918 |     \textrm{diam}\left(\coarseint{\strand_1}{D}{\strand_2}\right) \leq N(D),
0919 |   \] where the diameter of the empty set is 0.
0920 | \end{lem}
0921 | \begin{proof}
0922 |   Denote $G=\Isom{\waffle}$. Let $A \subset \waffle$ be a
0923 |   compact set such that $G A = \waffle$ (i.e. $A$ is a
0924 |   coarse fundamental domain) and let $\hat A = N_{2D}(A)$ be the $2D$
0925 |   neighbourhood of $A$.
0926 | 
0927 |   \emph{Claim:} Any pair $(\alpha,\beta)$ of strands of
0928 |   $\waffle$ such that $\coarseint \alpha D \beta \neq \emptyset$
0929 |   is in the same $G$-orbit as a pair of geodesics $(g\alpha,g\beta)$,
0930 |   which both intersect $\hat A$. Indeed, let $(\alpha,\beta)$ be such a
0931 |   pair, then there is some $x \in \waffle$ such that
0932 |   $d(x,\alpha),d(x,\beta) \leq D$. Let $g \in G$ be such that
0933 |   $gx \in A$. Then $g\alpha$ and $g\beta$ must intersect $\hat A$ in
0934 |   nonempty sets. The claim follows.
0935 | 
0936 |   We may therefore take
0937 |   \[N(D) = \max_{(\alpha,\beta)} M(\alpha,\beta,D)\] where
0938 |   $(\alpha,\beta)$ ranges over the pairs of strands that intersect
0939 |   $\hat A$, and $M(\alpha,\beta,D)$ is given in Lemma
0940 |   \ref{lem:coarse-int-finite}. This must be finite since there are
0941 |   only finitely many strands that intersect $\hat A$ .
0942 | \end{proof}
