1169 | \section{Commensurability from discrete groupings}
1170 | \label{sec:commensurability}
1171 | For this section denote by $\chuwaf{\Gamma}$ the churro-waffle space
1172 | associated to $\Gamma$. Let $G = \Isom{\chuwaf{\Gamma}}$ denote the
1173 | full isometry group, which by construction coincides with the
1174 | automorphism group of $\chuwaf\Gamma$ as a cell
1175 | complex. $\chuwaf{\Gamma}$ has the underlying structure of a tree of
1176 | spaces, dual to the JSJ splitting of $\Gamma$, denote this tree by
1177 | $T$, recall that this exactly the tree $\Tree{\gog J}$ constructed in
1178 | Proposition \ref{prop:covering-complex} item \ref{it:That-tree!} $T$
1179 | is bipartite with vertices either corresponding to waffles
1180 | (i.e. cubings of crêpes) or to churros. The
1181 | edges of $T$ correspond to the intersections of churros and waffles
1182 | along strands. It follows that vertex groups are waffle and churro
1183 | stabilizers and edge groups are the stabilizers of churro flaps. If
1184 | $v$ is a vertex of $T$ then the vertex group $G_v$, in general, is a
1185 | non-discrete totally disconnected locally compact group. On the other
1186 | hand the automorphism groups of churros and waffles are discrete. We
1187 | therefore denote by $\restr{G_v}$ the image of $G_v$ in the discrete
1188 | isometry group obtained by forgetting the action outside of those
1189 | subspaces.
