1368 | Denote by $\restr{G_\churro} =Z_\churro \leq \aut{\churrocore}$ the image of
1369 | $G_\churro$ in a discrete group of isometries of the real line. $Z_\churro$ is
1370 | either isomorphic to $\bbZ$ in which case it is said to be of
1371 | \define{$\bbZ$-type}, otherwise $Z_\churro$ is infinite dihedral and said to
1372 | be of \define{$\dihedralt$-type.} Let $\{\flap_1,\ldots,\flap_k\}$ be
1373 | a minimal set of representatives of $G_\churro$ orbits of
1374 | the set of flaps attached to $\churrocore$.
