1376 | For each $\flap_i$ we will construct a $Z_\churro$-orbit. By
1377 | construction there is a well-defined action of $Z_\churro$ on
1378 | $\churroclass{\flapfam{\flap_i}}$, the churro class of a flap
1379 | family. Denote by
1380 | $\rho_{\flap_i}:Z_\churro \to
1381 | \mathrm{Perm}\left(\churroclass{\flapfam{\flap_i}}\right)$ the
1382 | corresponding permutation representation, and denote the images
1383 | $\rho_{\flap_i}(g) = \bar g$. We can now express
1384 | $G_\churro\cdot \flap_i$ as a disjoint union of flap families
